    airo:evidenceText "[2198] Facebook's track record with content available on its platform..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2198" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c5358d4d0849> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sister platform Instagram is no stranger to the problem either, as it recently received a stern warning for allowing the online drugs trade to thrive." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2198" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c66a2d047b0d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Amy VanDeVelde is the national technology program director for Connections, a branch of The Oasis Institute, a St. Louis-based nonprofit that teaches older adults digital literacy and cybersecurity skills." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2200" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c6fbc792f9f3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Facebook’s Latest Scandal: Exposing Low Digitally Skilled Users to More Violent and Adult Content" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2121" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d38d5b693ea1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the Wall Street Journal detailed the extent to which Facebook’s artificial-intelligence systems are tripped up by various forms of disturbing content." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2199" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d534fe3cdd9b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2200] Facebook researchers conducted a five-question survey designed to assess its users' digital literacy skills." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2200" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f705fe99b5a0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Facebook's track record with content available on its platform is nothing worth envying, but for users who are not well-versed with social media tools, the platform dished out more disturbing content that could be anything from graphically violent to sexual in nature." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2198" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f7de9921d914> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Users with lower digital literacy tended to heavily use Facebook's Watch, a curated feed of popular and viral videos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2200" .

